  <!-- How to Choose -->
  <h2 id="how-to-choose">How to Choose the Right Standing Desk</h2>
  <p>
    So many options. Here's how to narrow down the right standing desk for your specific needs.
  </p>

  <h3>By Budget</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Under $300:</strong> Fezibo on Amazon, FlexiSpot E5 on sale.<br/>
    <strong>$300-500:</strong> FlexiSpot E7, Autonomous Desk Pro.<br/>
    <strong>$500-700:</strong> Uplift V3 base, Branch Duo, Vari, IKEA MITTZON.<br/>
    <strong>$700 plus:</strong> Uplift V3 upgraded, Secretlab Magnus Pro, Herman Miller Jarvis.
  </p>

  <h3>By Primary Need</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Best overall:</strong> Uplift V3, can't go wrong.<br/>
    <strong>Best value:</strong> FlexiSpot E7, premium features at reasonable price.<br/>
    <strong>Best budget:</strong> Autonomous Desk Pro, dual motor under $500.<br/>
    <strong>Best build quality:</strong> Herman Miller Jarvis, premium throughout. Buy it on sale.<br/>
    <strong>Best for small spaces:</strong> Vari Electric, T-leg design.<br/>
    <strong>Best design:</strong> Branch Duo, aesthetic focus.<br/>
    <strong>Best for gaming:</strong> Secretlab Magnus Pro, cable management.<br/>
    <strong>Best under $400:</strong> FlexiSpot E5, dual motor budget pick.
  </p>

  <h3>By User Height</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Under 5'4":</strong> FlexiSpot E7 at 22.8 inch min, Uplift V3 at 22.6 inch min.<br/>
    <strong>5'4" to 6'2":</strong> Any desk works. Uplift V3 or FlexiSpot E7 recommended.<br/>
    <strong>Over 6'2":</strong> Autonomous Desk Pro, 52 inch max height. Skip the Uplift V3 if you're very tall.
  </p>

  <h3>By Setup Weight</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Light setups like laptop plus monitor:</strong> Any desk works. Consider Fezibo for budget.<br/>
    <strong>Medium setups with dual monitors plus laptop:</strong> FlexiSpot E5 or better, Autonomous, Vari.<br/>
    <strong>Heavy setups with triple monitors and heavy equipment:</strong> Uplift V3, FlexiSpot E7, Herman Miller Jarvis. Need
    350 plus lb capacity.
  </p>

  <h3>Key Features to Consider</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Dual motors:</strong> Faster, quieter, more stable, longer-lasting. Worth the upgrade.<br/>
    <strong>Memory presets:</strong> One-touch height switching. Essential for daily standing.<br/>
    <strong>Anti-collision:</strong> Stops desk if it hits something. Protects equipment.<br/>
    <strong>Cable management:</strong> Built-in trays and routing. Keeps setup clean.<br/>
    <strong>Coverage:</strong> Ten plus years indicates confidence in quality.
  </p>

